WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:06.174
You learned the interactive revocation
list limits, twenty megabytes for

3
00:00:06.174 --> 00:00:11.387
GCC and forty-five for GCC High, with
ten seconds to download in every cloud.

4
00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:12.944
You measured three lists,

5
00:00:12.944 --> 00:00:16.874
and the missing one became a
recorded finding instead of a crash.

6
00:00:16.874 --> 00:00:20.565
You checked a fictional tenant
for GCC and then for GCC High,

7
00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:25.687
and saw how the cloud's limit changes the
findings while the download limit doesn't.

8
00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:28.783
Keep the measurement and
the check running every day,

9
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:32.300
because a list that fits today
can cross the limit next month.

10
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.646
Next is Module 6, time
separations from the logs:

11
00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:40.450
separation-to-block and
separation-to-revocation for every leaver.

12
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.487
It builds on this module,
because a card's revocation

13
00:00:43.487 --> 00:00:46.150
reaches sign-in through
the revocation list.
